        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ... and `stopinsert` is the only thing that seems to work for all the modes I could think of and also doesn't trigger `InsertEnter`\r\n\r\nAlmost :) It doesn't seem to work in Command mode. Based on documentation, `<C-\\><C-n>` is *the* way to ensure Normal mode (\"Additionally the command `CTRL-\\ CTRL-N` or `<C-\\><C-N>` can be used to go to Normal mode from any other mode.  This can be used to make sure Vim is in Normal mode, without causing a beep like <Esc> would.\").\r\n\r\n@treywood, I've just pushed [starter-ensure-normal](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/tree/starter-ensure-normal) branch. It has passing test for not triggering `InsertEnter`, but could you test it on your side, please?",
